###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The MLIP whose errors are analysed is not named in the main text or the SI read (only 'deep neural network' models with latent features); without an architecture no run can be attached to a registry method.
# - Error distributions, KS-test p-values, precision/recall/F1 sweeps and active-learning dataset sizes are shown in figures; the one error scale stated ('roughly 1 eV/A' as the instability cutoff) is a threshold, not a metric.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/annevelink2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
